jordan: Opened a small docs PR to add rate-limit backoff examples and update alerting panel links. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/5612

tara: Nice. Can you paste the minimal JS retry snippet and the console panel path? I'll polish language.

jordan: Snippet (in PR) shows exponential jitter backoff for 429s plus reading `x-redwood-rate-limit` headers to adapt retries. Also added a short note about alert thresholds in the console. JS snippet:

```js
// simple retry with exponential jitter reading rate-limit headers
async function callWithBackoff(fn) {
  let attempt = 0;
  while (attempt < 5) {
    const res = await fn();
    if (res.status !== 429) return res;
    const limit = res.headers.get('x-redwood-rate-limit') || 'unknown';
    const backoff = Math.min(1000 * 2 ** attempt, 10000) + Math.floor(Math.random() * 300);
    console.log(`429 received, header=${limit}, sleeping ${backoff}ms`);
    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, backoff));
    attempt++;
  }
  throw new Error('rate-limited after retries');
}
```

kevin: Please add a short curl example showing how to inspect headers and a one-liner for the Python SDK. Also we should clarify whether `x-redwood-rate-limit` reflects per-route or per-org caps.

jordan: Added curl + Python one-liners. Added text: "x-redwood-rate-limit reports the active cap scope (route/org) and a remaining token estimate; use it to adapt backoff windows."

